    <p style="margin-top: 2%;">
      Welcome to my website! I am a software engineer excited to provide pleasant user experiences with my work. 
      My journey from teaching mathematics and coding to becoming an engineer at tech companies has given me a unique perspective on problem-solving and creating better designs.
      <br><br>
      Here lies the portfolio of some of the things I did, particularly as an Undergraduate student in University of Toronto Scarborough which was when I wrote this website, and a few things about my work experience since then.  
      <br><br>
      I was inspired by my teachers who turned on figurative lightbulbs in my head; I still remember the curiosity I felt when I was shown mind-boggling ideas, 
      the eureka moment I felt when I struggled to make sense of a question in my assignment and my teacher patiently guided me through each step, the satisfaction I felt when I conquered the ridiculously challenging test written by my teacher.
      These precious memories has helped me navigate through different aspects in life, including my career.
      <br><br>
      During the year working as a secondary teacher, I created many learning materials for my classes and noted how well the students responded to the material in order get as many students to understand the difficult concepts of coding as I could. 
      For example, with Jupyter Notebooks that have long and detailed paragraphs, students became impatient with reading the materials; after adding more diagrams to illustrate a concept, breaking down paragraphs to 1-2 sentences and making more tiny practice checkpoints, 
      the students were more engaged in class and began to fill out the questions ahead of time. The moments when they respond with joy that they understand a new concept brings me fulfillment.
      <br><br>
      However, I was struggling to handle all the responsibilities as a teacher in that school and my personal life all at once. So I switched jobs to become a software developer, 
      a role that I have experiences on during my studies in university. Through the projects I worked on, I gained experiences on various roles in software development: Front End, Back End and DevOps, 
      which allows me to pick up different kinds of technical tasks quickly.
      In my spare time, I practice yoga, create music covers and make hand crafts (I however does not post proof on social media). 
    </p>

